{
  "name": "Understanding v1 semantic benchmark",
  "version": "2026-10-13",
  "purpose": "Diverse robot URLs with expected facts, used to score robot_understanding_v1 extraction and match_robot_url_v1 before switching v1 to default. 'matches' here means BUYER OPPORTUNITIES (companies likely to buy or pilot this robot for a workflow), never labor job postings.",
  "how_to_use": [
    "1. Confirm each URL resolves (HTTP 200) before running; flag any that redirect or 404. Entries marked verified=false come from general knowledge, not a live check.",
    "2. Run match_robot_url_v1 on each URL. Record extracted facts, derived capabilities, and top buyer verticals.",
    "3. Score: product_class correct? >=2 expected capabilities derived? at least one expected buyer vertical in the top matches? Any must_not_match vertical present = fail.",
    "4. Map the plain-English capability names below to our ontology terms; if a term has no ontology equivalent, list it as a gap rather than dropping it.",
    "5. The language_traps field lists phrasings the page is likely to use INSTEAD of the obvious keyword. These are the cases regex misses and semantic extraction must catch."
  ],
  "robots": [
